# STACK (LIFO)  (Structures / linear)
#
# MENTAL MODEL
#   A pile where you can only touch the top. Last in, first out. The reason
#   it appears everywhere is that it mirrors nesting — function calls,
#   brackets, undo history, and any 'most recent unmatched thing' question.
#
# INVARIANT
#   The only accessible element is the one most recently pushed and not yet
#   popped.
#
# COMPLEXITY  best O(1) push | avg O(1) pop | worst O(1) peek
# SPACE       O(n)
#
# REACH FOR IT WHEN
#   Anything with nesting or backtracking: expression parsing, DFS, undo,
#   monotonic-stack problems.
#
# AVOID WHEN
#   You need access to the oldest element — that is a queue.
#
# PITFALLS
#   1. Pop and peek on an empty stack must raise, not return None: None is a
#      legitimate stored value and silently conflating them hides bugs.
#   2. Array-backed pop from the END is O(1); popping from index 0 is O(n)
#      and turns the structure into a slow queue.
#   3. Recursion IS an implicit stack. Converting recursion to iteration
#      means making that stack explicit, which is the usual follow-up.
#
# SEE ALSO    queue, my_array, traversals, singly_linked_list
#
# INTERVIEW
#   - Valid Parentheses (LC 20)
#   - Min Stack (LC 155)
#   - Daily Temperatures (LC 739) — monotonic stack
#   - Largest Rectangle in Histogram (LC 84)
